```c
cleanup:
    if (curargv) {
        while(argc--)
            sdsfree(curargv[argc]);
        hi_free(curargv);
    }

    sdsfree(curarg);
    hi_free(cmd);

    return error_type;
```

No, `*target` is never set to NULL. So after a failure, `*target` retains its previous value (which is uninitialized in the fuzzer).

So the PoC is simply a string that causes `redisFormatCommand` to fail. The simplest way is to include an invalid format specifier like `%q`.

